ngerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Ghb","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Ghb / gbl","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Details of this combination are not well understood but PCP generally interacts in an unpredictable manner."},{"substance":"MAOIs","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MDMA","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"SSRIs","status":"Unsafe","tone":"danger","note":"Documented unsafe interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Tramadol","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Αmt","status":"Dangerous","tone":"danger","note":"Documented dangerous interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Caffeine","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"MXE","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"Opioids","status":"Caution","tone":"warning","note":"Uncertain or unpredictable interaction on PsychonautWiki."},{"substance":"2C-x","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"Cannabis","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"DMT","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"Ketamine","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"LSD","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"Mescaline","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"Mushrooms","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"NBOMes","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."},{"substance":"Nitrous","status":"Synergy","tone":"info","note":"TripSit classification: Low Risk & Synergy."}],"citations":[],"helpfulLinks":[{"title":"PsychonautWiki","description":"Pharmacology, subjective effects, and dosage reference","url":"https://psychonautwiki.org/wiki/PCP"},{"title":"TripSit Factsheet","description":"Rapid harm-reduction summary and combination data","url":"https://drugs.tripsit.me/pcp"},{"title":"Erowid Experience Vaults","description":"First-person experience reports and archives","url":"https://www.erowid.org/experiences/subs/exp_PCP.shtml"},{"title":"Wikipedia","description":"Encyclopedia article","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phencyclidine"},{"title":"Wikidata","description":"Structured data on PCP","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q407324"}],"wikidata":"Q407324","pharmacology":{"text":"PCP is well known for its primary action on the NMDA receptor, an ionotropic glutamate receptor. As such, PCP is a non-competitive NMDA receptor antagonist. The role of NMDAR antagonism in the effect of PCP, ketamine, and related dissociative agents was first published in the early 1980s by David Lodge and colleagues. Other NMDA receptor antagonists include ketamine, tiletamine, dextromethorphan, nitrous oxide, and dizocilpine (MK-801).","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Phencyclidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phencyclidine#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"NMDA receptor antagonists; General anesthetics; Dissociative hallucinogens","body":[{"what":"halfLife","says":"7–46 hours"},{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Oxidative hydroxylation in liver by CYP450 enzymes, glucuronidation"},{"what":"turnsInto","says":"PCHP, PPC, PCAA"},{"what":"leaves","says":"Urine"}],"figures":"Phencyclidine"},"uses":{"text":"Phencyclidine or phenylcyclohexyl piperidine (PCP), also known in its use as a street drug as angel dust among other names, is a dissociative anesthetic mainly used recreationally for its significant mind-altering effects. As a recreational drug, it is typically smoked, but may be taken by mouth, snorted, or injected. PCP is most commonly used in the US.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Phencyclidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phencyclidine","routes":"Smoking, injection, snorted, by mouth","figures":"Phencyclidine"},"sideEffects":{"text":"Adverse effects may include paranoia, addiction, and an increased risk of suicide, as well as seizures and coma in cases of overdose.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"Phencyclidine","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phencyclidine"}}